          "description": "<p><strong><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-attachment-id=\"19439\" data-permalink=\"https://events.fitnyc.edu/event/exhibition-architecting-the-future-of-creative-intelligence-opens/ctd-2026-poster-approved/\" data-orig-file=\"https://events.fitnyc.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/CTD-2026-Poster-Approved.png\" data-orig-size=\"450,800\" data-comments-opened=\"0\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"CT&amp;#038;D 2026 Poster Approved\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-medium-file=\"https://events.fitnyc.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/CTD-2026-Poster-Approved-225x400.png\" data-large-file=\"https://events.fitnyc.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/CTD-2026-Poster-Approved.png\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-19439 size-full\" src=\"https://events.fitnyc.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/CTD-2026-Poster-Approved.png\" alt=\"poster for Architecting the Future of Creative Intelligence with title of exhibition spelled out in brightly colored letters taking up the whole space of the poster \" width=\"450\" height=\"800\" srcset=\"https://events.fitnyc.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/CTD-2026-Poster-Approved.png 450w, https://events.fitnyc.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/CTD-2026-Poster-Approved-225x400.png 225w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px\" />October 16–November 8<br />\n</strong><strong>Goodman Center Lobby</strong></p>\n<p>The role of the designer is being redefined. As advanced technologies transform the design process, designers are moving beyond executing production details to become visionaries who shape ideas, direct systems, and orchestrate collaboration between humans and AI agents.</p>\n<p>This exhibition imagines a future where creative intelligence (CI) is measured not by what designers can produce with their own hands, but by what they can envision, direct, and bring to life. Freed from traditional production constraints, designers can focus on what matters most: asking better questions, solving bigger problems, and architecting meaningful solutions that were once beyond the reach of any individual.</p>\n<p><em>Architecting the Future o",
